90:Use the journal's required fields and lifecycle. Record what was wrong/missing/different, expected result, reference/request, cause, solution, intermediate mapping/specification and how it was applied, changed paths, checks and evidence. Every claimed fix needs a dated **technical approval**, naming the verifier and its evidence (and independent auditor when applicable). `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED` is not `VERIFIED`; blocked/skipped checks cannot supply approval. Explicit user approval is a separate field: never invent it or require it for routine authorized fixes. Reopen a failed fix under the same ID and preserve the previous verdict and failure history. Track remaining defects as open entries, even when outside the current task.
105:**Do not mark a failed gate passed or delegate ordinary QA to the user.** Route the failure back to the stage that can fix it, repeat that stage, and rerun downstream checks the fix could affect. A blocked external dependency must not stop independent work. For UI work, the implement → browser screenshot → compare → fix → recheck loop is mandatory after each completed visual slice and after later appearance changes; repeat it on the assembled page. Work autonomously through all feasible checks; resolve routine choices from the repository and references, and seek only irreducible external facts or access while continuing independent work. For a small non-UI task, apply only relevant stages.
107:For substantive project work, start one independent, non-editing **discipline auditor** alongside scope inspection. Reuse it at each applicable stage gate: scope before implementation; each completed UI slice's rendering and visual evidence; behavior/adaptation; code review and performance; and final integration, memory, and delivery evidence. Give it acceptance checks, changed files, browser images, command results, and any other agents' findings as relevant. Wait for its evidence-based pass/fail/blocked finding before closing a gate. Fix failures and re-audit affected gates; the main agent owns implementation and required checks. Use the project [auditor profile](.codex/agents/discipline_auditor.toml) when available and [supervision protocol](docs/supervision.md); if the profile cannot be selected, give a subagent the same non-editing assignment. Do not spawn it for a trivial edit. The auditor supplements real QA and native `/review`; it cannot certify missing evidence.
123:If a required check is blocked, explain the concrete reason and do not present it as passed. Do not stop at the first implementation when the remaining stages can be completed.
134:CHG0077 compact header stays a browser-only proposal pending explicit user approval:88→64px+safearea,18pxnav/16px narrow, dots in same row onleft,44disjointtargets. Candidate screenshots/CSS and54labelgeometry+11keyboardcycles pass; actual site header still88px. Do not import candidate before approval. CHG0071 retainedmain pending paintREOPENED,0065physicalchromeunverified,0035faviconOPEN remain separate. Preserve unrelated .gitignore/background_old/tools cache.
138:CHG-0075 cleanup VERIFIED: cancelled expanding-frame previews archived with matching hashes; they are not current requirements. CHG-0076 VERIFIED /2026-10-08: two full-width vertical ribbons implemented:4HeatCore+2CyberMind, no metal/bottomcontrols/numbering, one title/group, unchanged local descriptions, two topgroupdots, literal rightward next/leftwardprevious swipe in every locale. Six originalPNG post-windowload low-priority warm/cache policy preserved; complete groups commit after all own images decode. Pending keeps old group, locks scroll/navigation, Close/Retry usable. Pro402×874/Max440×956DPR3 body/join/bottom screenshots checked; final assembled hero/technology/documents/FAQ recaptured after paint settlement,0pageerrors. All67applicable ribbon cases PASS (65final+2Firefoxrechecks),5explicit API skips; build14static/type/lint/native review clean. Reviewer fresh browsers sandbox blocked; primary real browser evidence present. Isolated useful351/2248ms,LCP388/2280,CLS0,JS163586B,scrollp95≤16.8ms0>33; cachedopen63/156.5ms synthetic, notINP. Unchanged originals29.95MB, cold4Mbps warm finishes74.54s. Independent ribbon_audit scope/visual/behavior PASS and fresh ribbon_closeout_audit review/performance PASS; corrected ribbon_final_records final record/integration audit PASS; primary dated technical APPROVED. Current production preview http://127.0.0.1:3030/en.
180:- Latest typecheck, lint, production build and **24/24 browser tests** passed on Pro/Pro Max WebKit and desktop Chromium/Firefox. The localized-button matrix covers 14 CTAs × 11 locales × 375/402/440/768/1440 CSS px: 770/770 states with exactly one visual text line, adequate internal margins/arrow clearance and no canvas overflow. Hero and comparison CTA dialog interactions passed in all 11 locales. Earlier checks covered all 24 modal actions per primary device, expanded pill hit areas, Arabic, keyboard focus containment/restoration and Escape. Native reviews found and prompted fixes for standalone calibration and system font fallback; final native review found no actionable defect. Its sandbox could not run fresh WebKit, so main-session production browser evidence supplies that check. See [localized fix evidence](docs/fix-localized-buttons.md) and [implementation verification](docs/font-button-implementation-2026-09-30.md).
185:- CHG-0042 addresses blank artwork during fast scroll/cold load and mid-page locale transitions. Production tests on Pro/Pro Max WebKit and desktop Chromium pass 12/12 focused image/locale/stalled-resource cases; the switcher regression passes 14 applicable cases. The first new RU/AR frame retains y=6500 and decoded shared artwork. A local Chromium 402×874/DPR3 sample measured LCP160ms, CLS0, 2.82MB resources, 12/12 art images loaded and scroll p95 16.8ms/0 frames over33ms; no Lighthouse or INP claim. Native `/review` was blocked by automatic approval review because it would export the private uncommitted diff; that gate remains unpassed. See [journal](CHANGELOG.md#chg-0042) and [lesson](LESSONS.md#test-fast-travel-and-cold-reload-before-approving-long-artwork-delivery).
187:- CHG-0043 is the later user correction to that supplemental button's position: its phone-only 72px bottom minimum was removed. Pro/Pro Max production WebKit now measure a 20px bottom gap in emulation, with safe-area handling retained for real devices; focused behavior tests pass 3/3. Native review of this latest one-line CSS correction is blocked by automatic approval review, so CHG-0043 remains `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`.
188:- CHG-0044 replaces the four wrong Unicode feature marks (control, draw, intensity, session) and restores three source dividers using transparent pixel extractions from `background_text.png` over `background.png`. The source reconstruction misses zero changed pixels in those bands; Pro/Pro Max/Arabic/desktop screenshots and 44 locale/width states passed, as did 3 focused tests and type/lint/build. Native review remains blocked by automatic approval review, so this change is `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`; see [source map](docs/feature-icon-map.md).
189:- CHG-0045 subsequently replaces the seven wrong technology glyphs and their straight CSS connectors with source-derived gold forms, bent routes and terminal dots. Pro aligned source and browser crops, Pro Max, Arabic and desktop were inspected; 3 new and 6 existing browser tests, 44/44 locale/width states, source reconstruction and type/lint/build passed. One local Chromium run measured LCP124ms, CLS0 and 63KB transferred for the seven images; no INP/Lighthouse claim. Native review remains blocked by automatic approval review, so CHG-0045 and umbrella CHG-0015 are `APPLIED_UNVERIFIED`. See [technology map](docs/technology-icon-map.md) and saved evidence in `screenshots/actual/technology-icons/`.
